      "severity": "FAIL",
      "title": "Compare stored login eligibility rather than organization-aware eligibility",
      "description": "The original model comes from `getById()`, which wraps `isEnabled()` to return false when its organization is disabled. However, the cached login query is populated through the JPA delegate using the provider\u2019s stored enabled flag, independently of organization status.\n\nConsequently, populate the login cache, disable the organization, and then hide one of its providers on login. Both predicates here return false\u2014the original because the organization is disabled, the update because `hideOnLogin` is true\u2014so invalidation is skipped. Re-enabling the organization does not invalidate the login-query cache, and `OrganizationAwareIdentityProviderBean` only rechecks `isEnabled()`, allowing the now-hidden provider to appear again.\n\nCompare unwrapped, persisted eligibility for both models. Add a regression test covering an eligibility-changing update while the organization is disabled, followed by re-enabling it.",
      "file_ref": null,
      "category": "correctness",
      "raw_category": null,
      "location": "model/infinispan/src/main/java/org/keycloak/models/cache/infinispan/idp/InfinispanIdentityProviderStorageProvider.java:403-406"
    },
    {
      "severity": "CONCERN",
      "title": "Cleanup targets a literal alias instead of the created providers",
      "description": "The new test registers cleanup for `\"alias\"`, but creates providers named `idp-alias-0` through `idp-alias-19`. The same mistake occurs for `idp-alias-20` at line 425. These callbacks therefore remove none of the created providers and instead request deletion of a nonexistent provider, potentially producing cleanup failures and contaminating subsequent tests.\n\nCapture each actual alias when registering cleanup, and use `\"idp-alias-20\"` for the separately created provider.",
      "file_ref": null,
      "category": "test-debt",
      "raw_category": null,
      "location": "testsuite/integration-arquillian/tests/base/src/test/java/org/keycloak/testsuite/organization/cache/OrganizationCacheTest.java:381"
    }
